<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.2.1.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">271</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Onboarding Business Partner Onboarding AF groups functions that enable the integration and/or interaction of the systems. processes, and personnel of business partners with those of a Service Provider.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Product Specification and Offering Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Product Specification and Offering Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.3.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">272</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Product Specification and Offering Management Business Partner Product Specification and Offering Management aggregate function groups functions that manage Business Partner's Product Specification and Offering onboarding and request for quotation.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Product Specification and Offering Onboarding -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Product Specification and Offering Onboarding">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.3.1.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">273</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Product Specification and Offering Onboarding Business Partner Product Specification and Offering Onboarding Aggregate Function collects information from Business Partners to onboard their Product Specifications and Offerings.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.4.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">274</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Management The Business Partner Management aggregate function functions enable the creation and updates of Business Partner information such as name, address, organization, site location, interlocutors and interlocutor roles (legal representatives). 
The term Business Partner is used in the broad sense: dealer, reseller, wholesales, content provider (e.g. TV on XDSL), other network operator for interconnection or roaming purpose, Logistic Operator, partner, service provider for the technical support and IT projects, etc.
When the CSP decides to work with a Business Partner, he is referenced and typified (Supplier or Supplier and Partner, or with regard to the contents of purchases). 
It also manages supplier lists, preferred suppliers lists and also suppliers' black list, with information such as name, address, etc.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Agreement Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Agreement Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.4.1.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">275</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Agreement Management The Business Partner Agreement Management Aggregate Function includes supplier products and offers description, including prices, negotiated with the supplier according to the RFP (RFQ) content.
These agreements can be more or less complex and include:
- Purchases of materials and/or service deliveries, with prices depending on quantity, volume discounts or penalties, etc.
- Revenue sharing conditions, depending on end-customers usages for example.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Role Repository Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Role Repository Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.4.1.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">276</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Role Repository Management The Business Partner Role Repository Management Aggregate Function enables to identify the relevant roles associated with a Party during the commercial relationship with a Supplier. 
The term Supplier is used in the broad sense: dealer, reseller, wholesales, content provider (e.g. TV on XDSL), other network operator for interconnection or roaming purpose, Logistic Operator, partner, service provider for the technical support and IT projects, 
When we decide to work with a supplier, he is referenced and typified (Supplier or Supplier and Partner, or with regard to the contents of purchases). Partner is a particular typology of Supplier.

The Business Partner Repository Management is also in charge of gathering financial information related to potential partners, partner groups and hierarchies.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Collect and Qualify Business Partner Information -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Collect and Qualify Business Partner Information">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.4.1.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">277</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Collect and Qualify Business Partner Information The Collect and Qualify Business Partner Information Aggregate Function concerns the management of our knowledge of the Business Partner to keep or produce an up-to-date, accurate and legally compliant Business Partner information view.
It will incorporate into the Business Partner Information view, all relevant information gathered through all contacts with the Business Partner and in particular his field of activity.
Business Partner Information from other sources may be gathered, which will build a better knowledge of the supplier.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Product Repository Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Product Repository Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.4.1.5</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">279</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Product Repository Management The Business Partner Product Repository Management Aggregate Function allows to manage the configuration and statuses of the offers and products ordered to the Business Partner, according to its Offer and Product catalogue descriptions and rules. It also manages relationships between Products bought to the Business Partner with the CSP's different level of installed base (Product, Know-How a.k.a CFS, Technical Solution a.k.a RFS and Resource).

This Aggregate Function allows:
-	The Order Capture process to instantiate or update offers and products ordered to the Business Partner, whatever their type (network product, bundle, device, ) or their marketing mode (rented, sold, ), with their configuration, their tariffs and discounts, and their status (initialized with a creation order)
-	The Order Delivery to update Offer and Product installed base status
-	Any process to read Offer and Product installed base (subscribed offers, configuration of installed products, installed tariffs and discount, statuses, ).</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Order Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Order Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.5.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">280</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Order Management Business Partner Order Management Aggregate Function groups functions that manage the order to supplier or partner and the control of their fulfillment.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Order Validation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Order Validation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.5.1.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">281</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Order Validation Business Partner Order Validation Aggregate Function receives Purchase Requisition, manages approvals and convert into Business Partner Order according to agreed commercial arrangements with Business Partner.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Order Repository Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Order Repository Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.5.1.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">282</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Order Repository Management The Business Partner Order Repository Management Aggregate Function tracks and manages the events and the lifecycle related to the Business Partner Order and to its items (e.g. : Order lines).</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Goods Receipt -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Goods Receipt">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.5.1.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">283</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Goods Receipt The Goods Receipt Aggregate Function manages suppliers goods receipt including goods receipt checking (quantity, working) and possible return.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Performance Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Performance Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.6.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">284</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Performance Management The Business Partner Performance Management aggregate function groups functions used to evaluate Business Partners performance such as Supplier Performance.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Performance Evaluation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Performance Evaluation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.6.1.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">285</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Performance Evaluation The main goal of the Business Partner Performance Evaluation Aggregate Function is to reduce purchase risk and maximize the overall value for the purchaser. It typically involves evaluation, at a minimum, business partner quality, cost competitiveness, potential delivery performance and technological capability. Some of the other criteria used in the preliminary evaluation of business partners include financial risk analysis, evaluation of previous performance, and evaluation of business partner provided information.
Other criteria on the ethics and the environment can be also taken into account.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Trouble Ticket Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Trouble Ticket Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.6.1.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">286</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Trouble Ticket Management Business Partner Trouble Ticket Management Aggregate Function manages Business Partner Trouble Tickets, sending and receiving information about BP Trouble tickets. It includes billing and settlement disputes.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Financial Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Financial Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.7.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">287</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Financial Management The Business Partner Financial Management aggregate function groups functions used to pay Business Partners.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Payment Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Payment Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.7.1.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">288</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Payment Management Business Partner Payment Management Aggregate Function handles payments in the area of Business Partner billing and settlement. It is in charge of implementing Payment according to due debt and assigning in bound as well as outbound payments to invoices and settlement.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Due Debt Matching -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Due Debt Matching">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.7.1.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">289</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Due Debt Matching Business Partner Due Debt Matching Aggregate Function permits, prior to payments, to perform controls matching the invoice, sent by the supplier, to the purchase orders or the planned invoice / settlement calculated by the CSP.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Invoice Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Invoice Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.7.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">290</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Invoice Management Business Partner Invoice Management aggregate function groups functions which manage the financial interface with the supplier or partner including invoice matching and settlement.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Invoice Matching -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Invoice Matching">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.7.2.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">291</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Invoice Matching The Business Partner Invoice Matching Aggregate Function permits, prior to payments, to perform controls matching the invoice, sent by the business partner, to the purchase orders over the period considered.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Invoicing -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Invoicing">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.7.2.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">292</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Invoicing The Business Partner Invoicing Aggregate Function produces invoices on behalf of a partner, for example in case of revenue sharing. These invoices represent negative revenue for the CSP and will allow the partner for cashing the corresponding payment.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Settlement Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Settlement Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.7.2.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">293</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Settlement Management The Settlement Management Aggregate Function is necessary when enterprises want to avoid multiple two-way financial flows, for example when : 
- the agreement with the supplier includes revenue sharing (ex : N&#176; contact)
- and/or when the CSP sells on behalf and collects the money for the partner. 
It permits invoices aggregation per partner (received invoices and produced invoices) using a settlement account. 
According to the balance amount of the settlement account, a payment is sent or requested by the CSP to the partner.  

Notice: Settlement notes and invoice notes are both sent to the partner even when only one financial transfer is performed.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Rating -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Rating">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.7.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">294</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Rating Business Partner Rating aggregate function groups functions which manage the rating part of the supplier or partner.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Bill Calculation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Bill Calculation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.7.3.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">295</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Bill Calculation The Supplier Bill Calculation Aggregate Function prepares all the bill items necessary for the invoicing process on behalf of a partner. 
It collects, and eventually aggregates, the relevant results of the rating function, for the partner and for a dedicated period. 
It can also involve bill items coming from other providers.
It can calculate penalties or bonus depending on global amounts (of revenue, of usage types, ) or apply complex tax rules.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Rating and Revenue Sharing -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Rating and Revenue Sharing">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.7.3.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">296</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Rating and Revenue Sharing Business Partner Rating and Revenue Sharing Aggregate Function is in charge of:

	- Business Partner Revenue Sharing Identification that identifies the relevant pricing rules (tariffs, discounts and penalties) to be applied according to Revenue Sharing Agreement.
	- Business Partner Revenue Sharing Enforcement that applies revenue sharing pricing rules to calculate what the CSP owes to the Business Partner and what is owed by the Business Partner to the CSP.


	- And Business Partner Settlement Management that calculates settlements amounts according to what the CSP owes to the Business Partner (for Offers bought to the BP and for Revenue Sharing) and what is owed by the Business Partner to the CSP (for what has been bought by the BP to the CSP and for Revenue sharing).


It is done for any type of charges:

	-  recurring charges
	-  one-time charges (installation fees,  )
	-  usage charges, based on unitary product usage records (CDR) or on previously aggregated usage records


This information can be necessary to validate the supplier invoice the CSP will receive, or to prepare an invoice on behalf of the partner, for example in case of revenue sharing (ex : settlement of 10% of the revenue billed by the CSP to his customers, for a set of contents, to his supplier).</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Welcome and Interaction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Welcome and Interaction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.8.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">297</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Welcome and Interaction Business Partner Welcome and Interaction aggregate function groups functions in charge of managing all interfaces between the company and Business Partners.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Interaction Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Interaction Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.8.1.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">298</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Interaction Management Business Partner Interaction Management Aggregate Function manages all contact events with Business Partners.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Relationship Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Business Partner Relationship Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">6.8.1.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">299</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Business Partner Relationship Management Business Partner Relationship Management Aggregate Function identifies potential partners and determines partners that best meet the enterprise's needs.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Financial Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Financial Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.4.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">300</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Financial Management Financial Management Aggregate Function contains functions that permit budget, treasury as well as employee expenses management.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Budget Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Budget Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.4.1.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">301</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Budget Management The Budget Management Aggregate Function basically includes: budget forecast, simulation and control. Then it permits analysis, organization and oversight of costs and expenditures for the CSP.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Workforce Operational Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Workforce Operational Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.4.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">302</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Workforce Operational Management This Aggregate Function groups functions which manage the teams operational detailed workload schedule.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Workforce Activity Tracking -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Workforce Activity Tracking">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.4.2.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">303</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Workforce Activity Tracking The Workforce Activity Tracking Aggregate Function permits on-the-fly analysis of work orders management and workforce activity - including subcontractor's activities. 

It produces reports and KPI such as 
- workload per type of activity, per team or individual
- wait of intervention per type of activity
- short term forecasts of activity, based on effective production 
- etc.
It permits to measure current efficiency and to identify over or under loaded calendars (ex: increase of field interventions on a specific area after storm damage).

These information can help to adapt the short term workforce calendars - through the dedicated function.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Workforce Organization -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Workforce Organization">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.4.2.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">304</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Workforce Organization The Workforce Organization Aggregate Function permits to enrich the description of the actors and the operational teams, with information necessary to apply assignment rules, such as :

	- Detailed skills, relevant for the activity type
	- Assignment to team(s) and availability level
	- Assignment to territories, sales channel, products lines (ex: FTTH, ), customers types (ex: Major Accounts, Mass Market Customers, )
	- etc.
</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Workforce Schedule Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Workforce Schedule Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.4.2.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">305</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Workforce Schedule Management The Workforce Schedule Management Aggregate Function permits to initiate and update staff calendars and availability per type of activity and possible carrying out models - at team and individual levels - according to criteria and rules.

The workload management schedule is first concerned by future requirements and is limited to capacity management - for internal teams and subcontractors. It uses mid-term activity forecasts.
The workload management schedule is then updated and detailed at teams and - if necessary - individuals levels to become operational (ex: for the next 2 weeks).

The scheduled can be adapted depending on Workforce Activity Tracking information. Adaptation may consist in allowing dispatching of staff from other geographical area or to other activities, adapt staff allocation per type of activity, hiring temporary manpower, increase subcontracting volume, </rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Workforce Appointment Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Workforce Appointment Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.4.2.4</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">306</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Workforce Appointment Management The Workforce Appointment Management Aggregate Function enables to manage Workforce appointment with any Party such as Customer, Business Partner. It takes into account the availability of the participants and tracks the appointment in the workforce calendar.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Bank Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Bank Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.4.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">307</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Bank Management Bank Management Aggregate Function is in charge of managing CSP's Bank Accounts.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Treasury Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Treasury Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.4.3.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">308</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Treasury Management The Treasury Management Aggregate Function consists in managing short or medium term cash-flow forecasts, financial investments for cash surplus as well as cash funding for company requirements.
It embeds the following sub-functions:
- daily cash flow position delivery, at short-term and medium-term
- cash flow budget management to forecast cash requirements or surplus
- certification and transmission of settlements or debit orders towards banks by the means of SWIFT or EBICS messages
- cash flows transfers accounting
- bank reconciliation
- foreign exchange rates management.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Enterprise Revenue Assurance -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Enterprise Revenue Assurance">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.6.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">309</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Enterprise Revenue Assurance The Revenue Assurance Management Aggregate Function includes functions which are in charge of defining company strategy and methods to minimize the revenue leakage.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Revenue Assurance Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Revenue Assurance Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.6.1.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">310</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Revenue Assurance Management The Revenue Assurance Aggregate Function handles all the actions having for target to make sure, the procedures and the practices implemented by the company, that all the incomes expected from products supplied to the customers are invoiced, recovered and registered in an exhaustive and exact way.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Revenue Assurance Problem Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Revenue Assurance Problem Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.6.1.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">311</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Revenue Assurance Problem Management Revenue Assurance Problem Management Aggregate Function identifies, tracks and solve Revenue Assurance Problems and initiate recovery of the lost revenue.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Revenue Assurance Rules Definition -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Revenue Assurance Rules Definition">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.6.1.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">312</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Revenue Assurance Rules Definition Revenue Assurance Rules Definition Aggregate Function establishes the policies and rules to be applied to the Revenue Assurance process.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Assurance -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Assurance">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.6.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">313</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Human Resource Assurance Human Resource Assurance Aggregate Function groups functions in charge of defining, analyzing and reporting short and long terms goals for employees.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Performance Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Performance Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.6.2.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">314</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Human Resource Performance Management Human Resource Performance Management Aggregate Function supports defining and evaluating goals for personnel.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Accounting Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Accounting Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">315</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Accounting Management Accounting Management Aggregate Function contains functions which allow one to manage the accounting of the company.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.General Ledger -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.General Ledger">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.1.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">316</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">General Ledger The General Ledger Aggregate Function provides a central repository for all financial transactions and statistical information. It is at the core of accountancy. In general, it permits to define a multi-company, multi-divisional, multi-currency ledger.
- Natural accounts management (e.g. Account 401 to aggregate all the auxiliaries suppliers 401xxx)
- Posting in Control Accounts + other accounts
- Enter journals, upload journals
- Reversal of journals (i.e.: accruals)
- Open and Close GL Periods
- Foreign currency Revaluation and Translation
- Cost and Revenue breakdown
- Reporting and analysis.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Lease Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Lease Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.1.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">317</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Lease Management Lease Management Aggregate Function manages Capital Lease for Complete contract tracking and reporting.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Subledger Accounting -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Subledger Accounting">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.1.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">318</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Subledger Accounting An auxiliary account is one subdivision of a general account and concerns a third party account. It leans on an auxiliary journal which collects the credit / debit events. There are:
- a purchase journal
- a sales journal 
- banks journals (one per bank)
- a cash book
- a miscellaneous transaction journal
- a payroll journal.

The auxiliary feeds periodically the general accounting under the shape of a single centralized aggregated book entry. 
The Subledger Accounting Aggregate Function:
- limits the number of book entry by third party account
- facilitates the accounting lettering
- helps to the preparation of the balance sheet
- favors the periodic accounting audit.

It includes the auxiliary Customer, Supplier and Stock accountancies.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Tax Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Tax Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.1.4</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">319</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Tax Management The Tax Management Aggregate Function assures:
- taxes declarations and particularly VAT 
- legal reports management
- fiscal rules definition and the control of the application of these rules, including by the tax authorities.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Regulatory Accounting -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Regulatory Accounting">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.1.5</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">320</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Regulatory Accounting Regulatory Accounting Aggregate Function is in charge of managing cost allocations, affiliate billing and international settlements according to Regulatory Accounting rules.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Expense Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Expense Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">321</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Human Resource Expense Management Human Resource Expense Management Aggregate Function cover the treatment of employees expenses such as payroll and travel expenses.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Travel Expense Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Travel Expense Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.2.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">322</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Travel Expense Management Travel Expense Management Aggregate Function collects Employees' expense including electronic attachments. It also manages the approval of expenses, the expense reimbursements and integration with accounts payable.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Asset Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Asset Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.4</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">323</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Asset Management The Asset Management Aggregate Function mainly enables one to:
- manage all the resources which are used and shared within the company, namely the physical and financial assets deployed in the enterprise
- optimize the expected savings linked to these all along their lifecycle from their purchase and setup until their total depreciation or amortization.

This Aggregate Function embeds three functions:
- Corporate Real Estate Management
- Vehicle Fleet Management
- Intellectual Property Management

This Aggregate Function DOESN'T manage the Tangible and Intangible Products sold to the CUSTOMERS, only those used within the enterprise for its own needs.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Corporate Real Estate (Buildings) -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Corporate Real Estate (Buildings)">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.4.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">324</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Corporate Real Estate (Buildings) Corporate Real Estate Aggregate Function:
- Describes the real estate property held or used by a business enterprise or organization for its own operational purposes.
- May also describe the functional practices, organizations and professions that are concerned with the planning, acquisition, management, and administration of real property on behalf of a company.

Corporate real estate professionals handle real estate market exactly as corporate purchasing or procurement.
It includes the following functions : 
- Real Estate Facility Operations Management (FM) is an interdisciplinary field devoted to the co-ordination of all business support services. FM involves all types of business support processes including the care of offices, commercial or institutional buildings which are necessary to the operator and the employees. FM can be defined as the integration and alignment of the non-core services, including those relating to premises, required to operate and maintain a business to fully support the core objectives of the organization.
- Space planning function deals with the way to plan and organize required necessary space in buildings for operator activities. It embeds: offices, workrooms, shops, warehouses, telecom equipment centers, data centers, switch centers, corporate restaurants, and parking.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Intellectual Property Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Intellectual Property Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.4.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">325</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Intellectual Property Management Intellectual Property Management Aggregate Function manages the lifecycle of intellectual assets, their use and share.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Vehicle Fleet Management (Transport) -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Vehicle Fleet Management (Transport)">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.7.4.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">326</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Vehicle Fleet Management (Transport) Vehicle Fleet Management permits to manage company's vehicle fleet. 
Vehicle fleet is made of commercial motor vehicles such as cars, vans, trucks, boats etc.
Fleet (vehicle) management includes a set of functionalities, such as 
- Vehicle financing,
- Vehicle maintenance,
- Vehicle telematics (tracking and diagnostics),
- River management, speed management,
- Fuel management, 
- Health and safety management.

Fleet Management is a function which allows companies which rely on transportation in their business to remove or minimize the risks associated with vehicle investment, improving efficiency, productivity and reducing their overall transportation and staff costs, providing 100% compliance with government legislation (duty of care) and many more.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

