<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Patent and Invention Management Patent, Invention &amp; Trademark Management collects possible patent, invention and trademark candidates.
It also manages the registration process and making the knowledge available within the enterprise.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Administration, Compensation and Benefits Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Administration, Compensation and Benefits Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.5</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">335</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Human Resource Administration, Compensation and Benefits Management The Human Resource Administration, Compensation and Benefits Management Aggregate Function groups functions in charge of
1. processing and managing records and employees data, ensuring they are accurate and up-to-date, corresponding and taking into account any changes resulting from management decisions, legal and regulatory requirements and personal circumstances,
2. managing the individual Compensation and Benefits calculation, giving the instructions for the payroll process.
Note that for some countries (UK), the Information System must provide functions for pension funds and social security management.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Administration -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Administration">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.5.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">336</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Human Resource Administration Human Resource Administration Aggregate Function permits management of all legal and administrative employees data such as identity, contacts/addresses, contract of employment, job position (job profile, localization, management), etc.
Processes the registration of the new employees (hiring, mobility), updates personal situation (marital status, children, addresses, dependents / beneficiaries, etc) and professional situation, updates contracts status (termination, resignation, retirement).</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Communication Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Communication Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
