<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Human Resource Communication Management Human Resource Communication Management Aggregate Function supports Corporate Goals and Key initiatives communication and facilitates community programs.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Employee Relationship Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Employee Relationship Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.5.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">338</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Employee Relationship Management Employee Relationship Management Aggregate Function is in charge of all relationships between CSP and employees including advertising for recruitment.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Individual Remuneration Policy Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Individual Remuneration Policy Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.5.4</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">339</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Individual Remuneration Policy Management The Individual Remuneration Policy Aggregate Function manages the employees individual remuneration.
It represents the declension at employee level of the general company remuneration policy (fixed base salary, managerial bonus), the standard benefits and all other kind of benefits granted to the employee (profit sharing, stock options, shareholders program, car policy).

Subfunctions used:
- Compensation Management,
- Profit Sharing Management,
- Benefits Management.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Payroll Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Payroll Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.5.5</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">340</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Payroll Management The Payroll Aggregate Function permits to manage:
- employee payroll data applying the Individual Remuneration Policy and ensuring they are accurate and up-to-date, reflecting any changes resulting from management decisions, legal &amp; regulatory requirements and personal circumstances in order to provide payslips, payment, contributions, legal declarations, etc.
- the calculation of the payroll data
- the payment of the payroll.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Employee Repository Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Employee Repository Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.5.6</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">341</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Employee Repository Management Employee Repository Management Aggregate Function is in charge of managing employees information and identification means such as unique employee number and identification card.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Social Relationships Piloting -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Social Relationships Piloting">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.5.7</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">342</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Social Relationships Piloting Social Relationships Piloting Aggregate Function covers the piloting of the relationships with the employees representatives.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Working Time Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Working Time Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.5.8</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">343</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Working Time Management The Working Time Administration Aggregate Function manages all elements associated with time worked including overtime, night, weekend and home works management.
This function provides a consolidated situation of employees working time.
It allows the management of the working schedule, the overtime hours, the penalties, </rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Human Capital Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Human Capital Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.6</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">344</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Human Resource Human Capital Management Human Resource Human Capital Management Aggregate Function groups functions covering all the operations and data related to human resource and competencies development.
It covers, on one hand, the internal and external processes of recruitment, and, on the other hand, the processes contributing in the management of the performance and competencies which aims to improve individual performance and, by this way, to insure the achievement of Orange group's strategic business goals.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Evaluations and Career Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Evaluations and Career Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.6.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">345</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Evaluations and Career Management The Evaluation and Career Management Aggregate Function treats about individual management of career and performance of an employee.
Two main goals:
- First: improve individual performance of each employee all along his professional career
This goal relies on assessment processes consisting in a regular face to face meeting between employee and his manager in order to:

	- share and agree on individual goals,
	- measure employee performance results,
	- assess employee competencies and then, 
	-  identify training development actions.

- Second: manage and propose development career plan based upon competencies management 

	-  proceeding  to a follow-up of individual career data details to see and track individual career evolution,
	-  helping in displaying to employee internally needs that could match to employee wishes.


It is based upon a shared group master data referential managing Jobs and Competencies that is updated according to company policy strategy.
It gathers the following sub-functions:
- Setting (and sharing) individual Goals,
- Performance individual assessment,
- Company Jobs and Skills master data management 
- Gap assessment between awaited and owned employee competencies 
- Employee assignment to key company jobs.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.External and Internal (Mobility) Recruitment -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.External and Internal (Mobility) Recruitment">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.6.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">346</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">External and Internal (Mobility) Recruitment The External and Internal (Mobility) Recruitment Aggregate Function is in charge of finding, allocating and making ready the right resources at the right time to target areas of the business.
It consumes and stores standard CVs and provides services permitting selection of profiles (including interviews results, candidate choice). 
This function also provides job offer search and display. This function includes the mobility for internal applicants and covers internal mobility inside the same company of the CSP group or between companies of the CSP Group. Special transfers to national and local government services are also taken into account by this function. 
It includes Job Offer Management, Applicant Management, Job Application Management and Applicant Pre-Hiring.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Training Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Training Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.6.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">347</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Training Management The Training Management Aggregate Function addresses and manages the training functions in its globality from training elaboration and delivery to course assessment after course attending.
It permits to manage employee inscription to course session, courses assessment, etc 

It embeds the following sub-functions:
- Training plan management, 
- Training catalogue management, 
- Training Course session inscription management,
- External training purchasing
- Training delivery management.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Social Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Human Resource Social Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.7</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">348</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Human Resource Social Management Human Resource Social Management Aggregate Function groups functions covering all the operations and data related to social management.
It defines the policy for employees relations, health and safety, and corporate social responsibility. It supports managers in their implementation and control results.
Each company / country develops its own approach in employees relations, health and safety, work time and corporate social responsibility in coherence with group policies and local legal and mandatory requirements and agreements.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Safety and Working Environment Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Safety and Working Environment Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.7.1</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">349</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Safety and Working Environment Management This Aggregate Function permits to manage all the data necessary to ensure an even improving safety and working environment in compliance with legal requirements.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Social Protection Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Social Protection Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.7.2</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">350</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Social Protection Management This Aggregate Function covers the management or the taking account of the social protection systems: life insurance, disability insurances, employers liability insurances, occupational diseases insurances.
This function doesnt cover the financial part of the contracts and funds functioning operations. In all the countries, these operations and the associated managing system are directly provided by insurance companies.
Nevertheless, in some countries (UK), the CSP HR actors have to make specific operations and controls about social security contribution. These operations and controls are covered by the Social security management function in the HR Administration functional block.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Ethics & Compliance Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Ethics & Compliance Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
<TMF_v1:AFLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2</TMF_v1:AFLevel>
<TMF_v1:hasID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">7.10.7.3</TMF_v1:hasID>
<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">351</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Ethics & Compliance Management Ethics &amp; Compliance Management provides the following functionality:
- Provides a program to ensure Labor is properly trained on ethics and compliance requirements. 
- Provides a program to enable safe reporting of ethical and compliance violations. 
- Ensures company is meeting ethical and compliance standards. 
- Institutes and manages programs such as EEO case management to track violations.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Regulatory Rules Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF.Regulatory Rules Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AF"/>
